{"type":"standard","title":"Laurie Buckhout","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Laurie Buckhout</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q124749721","titles":{"canonical":"Laurie_Buckhout","normalized":"Laurie Buckhout","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Laurie Buckhout</span></span>"},"pageid":76271713,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Laurie_Buckhout.jpg/330px-Laurie_Buckhout.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":413},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e4/Laurie_Buckhout.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":3312,"height":4140},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1375221850","tid":"a091644f-b1dc-11f1-ac6f-9098f1cce622","timestamp":"2026-09-16T14:40:57Z","description":"American politician (born 1961)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laurie_Buckhout","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laurie_Buckhout?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laurie_Buckhout?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Laurie_Buckhout"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laurie_Buckhout","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Laurie_Buckhout","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laurie_Buckhout?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Laurie_Buckhout"}},"extract":"Laurie Moe Buckhout is an American politician and retired military officer. She served as Assistant Secretary of Defense for Cyber Policy in 2025. Buckhout is the Republican nominee in the 2026 election in North Carolina's 1st congressional district, having previously been their nominee for the same district in 2024.","extract_html":"<p><b>Laurie Moe Buckhout</b> is an American politician and retired military officer. She served as Assistant Secretary of Defense for Cyber Policy in 2025. Buckhout is the Republican nominee in the 2026 election in North Carolina's 1st congressional district, having previously been their nominee for the same district in 2024.</p>"}